ﬂÑˇˇ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀‰˝™Ñˇˇ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀"Sure! Here's a revised review of the diagnosis results and proposed solutions:\n\n## Review of the Diagnosis\n\n1. In the diagnosis report, it was noted that memory usage anomalies were addressed using metrics queries and workload matching. However, the report doesn't provide concrete data or specific anomalies in these metrics that led to this conclusion. Incorporating this data into the report can provide a more comprehensive diagnosis and solidify your evidence.\n\n2. High network activity metrics were mentioned without concrete details. To provide a clearer diagnosis, add specific metrics values and display how they fluctuate over time. Also, consider presenting how these metrics relate to the identified issue on hand.\n\n3. When diagnosing issues related to high memory usage, remember to consider various potential causes such as inefficient data handling, memory leaks, poor garbage collection, or improper database configurations. Your diagnosis should not only revolve around high network activity metrics.\n\n## Review of the Proposed Solutions\n\n1. The solution of 'Optimizing network operations' is quite general. Could you be more specific? Do you mean reconsidering the data packet size, varying the workload based on the network traffic patterns, or limiting the number of high memory consuming processes running concurrently? Please specify.\n\n2. Similarly, the recommendation to 'increase memory allocation' can sometimes act as a workaround instead of a solution. Consider diving deeper into memory management solutions such as introducing a caching system, optimizing data structures for low memory footprint or making improvements in garbage collection.\n\n3. Please recommend APIs or tools that can be used to implement these proposed solutions. This would offer more practical assistance which can be directly applied to resolve the identified issue.\n\n4. Lastly, a robust solution should incorporate preventive measures to avoid future occurrences of the identified issue. This might include configuring alert systems for memory usage thresholds, scheduling regular audits of resource-consuming processes or instituting automated tests to check for memory leaks. \n\nRemember, diagnosis and solutions should be specific, actionable, and evidence-based to ensure they are effective and reliable."␀ˇ␀␀0˛πÑˇˇ␀␀·í␀␀␀␀␀␀ç‚™™␀␀∞M‚™™␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀‰ú•Ñˇˇ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀"Thought: The alert status is resolved, and the alert description shows that there was high CPU usage on a node. I need to verify whether the CPU usage was truly abnormal during the alert period.<br><details open><summary><span style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold; color: #333333\">using Tools:</span></summary><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; line-height: 36px\"><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Command Name:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important;\">whether_is_abnormal_metric</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Arguments:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important; white-space: pre-wrap\">\"{\\\"start_time\\\": \\\"2023-10-15 15:04:49\\\", \\\"end_time\\\": \\\"2023-10-15 15:14:49\\\", \\\"metric_name\\\": \\\"cpu_usage\\\"}\"</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Command Status:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important;\">Success</div></div></div></details>"␀␀Åç␀␀␀␀␀␀0◊‚™™␀␀†
ﬂÑˇˇ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀‰75Á˛ˇ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀"The metric cpu_usage is abnormal <br>  <br> <img style=\"border-radius: 8px;\" src=\"data:image/jpg;base64,\">"␀˝™Ñˇˇ␀␀p!6Á˛ˇ␀␀ÒQ␀␀␀␀␀␀0◊‚™™␀␀†
ﬂÑˇˇ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀‰6Á˛ˇ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀"Thought: The CPU usage was indeed abnormal during the alert time period, hence confirming the alert. To further understand this anomaly, I will diagnose this with the cpu_match_diagnose_knowledge tool.<br><details open><summary><span style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold; color: #333333\">using Tools:</span></summary><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; line-height: 36px\"><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Command Name:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important;\">cpu_match_diagnose_knowledge</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Arguments:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important; white-space: pre-wrap\">\"{\\\"start_time\\\": \\\"2023-10-15 15:04:49\\\", \\\"end_time\\\": \\\"2023-10-15 15:14:49\\\", \\\"metric_name\\\": \\\"cpu\\\", \\\"alert_metric\\\": \\\"cpu_usage\\\", \\\"diag_id\\\": \\\"abc123\\\"}\"</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Command Status:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important;\">Success</div></div></div></details>"␀˛ˇ␀␀AL␀␀␀␀␀␀ç‚™™␀␀0◊‚™™␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀‰ú•Ñˇˇ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀"Thought: Based on the results from cpu_match_diagnose_knowledge, the root cause of the high CPU usage is abnormal patterns in `node_procs_running`, `node_procs_blocked`, and `node_entropy_available_bits`. The number of running processes jumped to 10 at maximum comparing to its mean of 2.44, indicating these processes might compete CPU resources. The blocked processes also displayed abnormal patterns. Moreover, node_entropy_available_bits varies significantly, it raises the question whether there are issues with system entropy which could indirectly affect the CPU usage. <br><br>Unfortunately, we cannot inspect the workload queries as the specific SQL queries executed during the anomaly are not available for analysis.<br><details open><summary><span style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold; color: #333333\">using Tools:</span></summary><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; line-height: 36px\"><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Command Name:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important;\">Speak</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Arguments:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important; white-space: pre-wrap\">\"{\\\"diagnose\\\": \\\"The root cause is identified as abnormal patterns in node_procs_running, node_procs_blocked and node_entropy_available_bits. However, due to lack of specific SQL queries, more detailed root cause cannot be determined.\\\", \\\"solution\\\": \\\"Closely monitor and limit resource intensive processes to prevent them from consuming a lot of CPU. If possible, balance your workload to ensure the load is evenly distributed over time.\\nNote: Without specific SQL queries, more detailed solutions cannot be given.\\\", \\\"knowledge\\\": \\\"Certain heavy workloads might result in high CPU usage if there is a sudden increase in the number of operating processes or blocked processes. Additionally, system entropy could have an indirect impact on CPU usage.\\\" }\"</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Command Status:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important;\">Success</div></div></div></details>"␀␀␀0˛πÑˇˇ␀␀QB␀␀␀␀␀␀êÄ‚™™␀␀†
ﬂÑˇˇ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀‰˛πÑˇˇ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀"Thought: Now that I have obtained the start and end time of the anomaly, check whether the memory usage is abnormal during that time period.<br><details open><summary><span style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold; color: #333333\">using Tools:</span></summary><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; line-height: 36px\"><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Command Name:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important;\">whether_is_abnormal_metric</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Arguments:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important; white-space: pre-wrap\">\"{\\\"start_time\\\": \\\"2023-10-15 15:04:49\\\", \\\"end_time\\\": \\\"2023-10-15 15:14:49\\\", \\\"metric_name\\\": \\\"memory_usage\\\"}\"</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Command Status:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important;\">Success</div></div></div></details>"␀˛ˇ␀␀!=␀␀␀␀␀␀êÄ‚™™␀␀†
