ﬂÑˇˇ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀‰˛πÑˇˇ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀"Thought: The cpu_usage metric was indeed abnormal during the alert time. Now, I need to identify the root cause of this high CPU usage anomaly using metrics, queries and knowledge gained from cpu_match_diagnose_knowledge.<br><details open><summary><span style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold; color: #333333\">using Tools:</span></summary><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; line-height: 36px\"><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Command Name:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important;\">cpu_match_diagnose_knowledge</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Arguments:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important; white-space: pre-wrap\">\"{\\\"start_time\\\": \\\"2023-10-15 14:37:49\\\", \\\"end_time\\\": \\\"2023-10-15 14:54:49\\\", \\\"metric_name\\\": \\\"cpu\\\", \\\"alert_metric\\\": \\\"cpu_usage\\\", \\\"diag_id\\\" : \\\"2023-10-15\\\"}\"</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Command Status:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important;\">Success</div></div></div></details>"␀ˇ␀␀pú•Ñˇˇ␀␀Ò-␀␀␀␀␀␀0_‚™™␀␀–ˆ‚™™␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀‰J7Á˛ˇ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀"Thought: From the information I gathered, it seems that there are a number of processes running and blocked which contributes to the CPU usage. The abnormal processes running might be due to queries like creating and dropping indexes, and updating tables. Therefore, optimizing this could be a good direction for resolving the high CPU usage. <br><br>First, the query that stood out is \"CREATE INDEX index_table1_i ON table1(namei);\", which was run multiple times. Creating indices can be CPU-intensive and can lock tables, potentially blocking other queries, and it is typically not an operation that should be frequently performed. <br><br>Secondly, I observed frequent updates to table1, which can also strain the system's resources. Depending on the change made, updates can potentially re-write large amounts of data, and their impacts on system load can vary greatly.<br><br>Considering these factors, the solution could be to optimize the index and update operations.<br><br><details open><summary><span style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold; color: #333333\">using Tools:</span></summary><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; line-height: 36px\"><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Command Name:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important;\">optimize_index_selection</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Arguments:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important; white-space: pre-wrap\">\"{\\\"start_time\\\": \\\"2023-10-15 14:37:49\\\", \\\"end_time\\\": \\\"2023-10-15 14:54:49\\\"}\"</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Command Status:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important;\">Success</div></div></div></details>"␀␀pú•Ñˇˇ␀␀°%␀␀␀␀␀␀‡≥‚™™␀␀†
ﬂÑˇˇ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀‰]7Á˛ˇ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀"Thought: Based on the optimized index suggestion, we can improve the system's performance by creating a single multi-column index on table1 for id, namei, and col_name. This index should be more efficient than creating multiple individual indices.<br><br>Additionally, for the frequent update operations on table1, it would be optimal to batch these update operations to reduce the number of times the table is accessed and data is rewritten.<br><br>Finally, regarding the entropy available bits metric, this is usually related to the randomness required for certain operations such as cryptographic functions, shuffling arrays, and generating unique identifiers. However, since this metric is fairly stable in its behaviour (no significant deviations found), it is less likely to be directly related to the current performance issue.<br><br>Let's calculate and apply these solutions to address the high CPU usage.<br><br><details open><summary><span style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold; color: #333333\">using Tools:</span></summary><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; line-height: 36px\"><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Command Name:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important;\">Speak</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Arguments:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important; white-space: pre-wrap\">\"{\\\"diagnose\\\": \\\"The high CPU usage is likely caused by frequent creation and dropping of indices, and frequent update operations on table1.\\\", \\n                \\\"solution\\\": \\\"1. Replace the frequently created index with the following: `CREATE INDEX index_table1 ON table1(id, namei, col_name);` \\n2. Batch the frequent update operations to reduce the strain on system resources.\\\",\\n                \\\"knowledge\\\": \\\"Creating and dropping indices frequently can cause high CPU usage due to its high resource-demanding nature. Updates can also influence the CPU usage depending on the amount of data being rewritten. Available entropy doesn't seem to contribute significantly to this issue based on its stable patterns.\\\"}\"</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Command Status:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important;\">Success</div></div></div></details>"␀ˇˇ␀␀p˝™Ñˇˇ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀‡≥‚™™␀␀†
