ﬂÑˇˇ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀‰∫2Á˛ˇ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀"Thought: It seems there's an issue with recognizing the \"workload_usage\" metric. Let's try another common metric for identifying anomalies, \"memory_usage\".<br><details open><summary><span style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold; color: #333333\">using Tools:</span></summary><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; line-height: 36px\"><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Command Name:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important;\">whether_is_abnormal_metric</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Arguments:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important; white-space: pre-wrap\">\"{\\\"start_time\\\": \\\"2023-10-15 14:37:49\\\", \\\"end_time\\\": \\\"2023-10-15 14:54:49\\\", \\\"metric_name\\\": \\\"memory_usage\\\"}\"</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Command Status:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important;\">Success</div></div></div></details>"␀␀a␀␀␀␀␀␀‡≥‚™™␀␀†
ﬂÑˇˇ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀‰˛πÑˇˇ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀"Thought: It seems there is a persistent issue with the recognition of the metrics. It may be due to the provided metrics not being supported or an issue with the API. To find the root cause of the performance issue, I'll need to use the 'workload_match_diagnose_knowledge' tool.<br><details open><summary><span style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold; color: #333333\">using Tools:</span></summary><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; line-height: 36px\"><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Command Name:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important;\">workload_match_diagnose_knowledge</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Arguments:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important; white-space: pre-wrap\">\"{\\\"start_time\\\": \\\"2023-10-15 14:37:49\\\", \\\"end_time\\\": \\\"2023-10-15 14:54:49\\\", \\\"metric_name\\\": \\\"ins:stdload1[ins=]\\\", \\\"alert_metric\\\":\\\"1.55\\\", \\\"diag_id\\\":\\\"\\\"}\"</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #333333; width: 160px; flex-shrink: 0\">Command Status:</div><div style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #676c90!important;\">Success</div></div></div></details>"␀a␀␀␀␀␀␀0_‚™™␀␀‡≥‚™™␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀‰™7Á˛ˇ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀"Thought: First, I need to determine whether there were abnormal metrics during the time of the anomaly by looking at the CPU usage.<br><details open><summary><span style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold; color: #333333\">using Tools:</span></summary><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; line-height: 36px\"><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-content: center\"><div style=\"font-size: 14